# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored - it holds a password,
# and this repository is public.
#
# Loaded automatically by every `mothman` command and by pytest, so
# there is nothing to export and no flag to remember. Anything already
# set in your shell WINS over this file, deliberately: CI supplies its
# own values, and a variable you just exported to try something should
# beat one you wrote here last month.
#
# The session hook (.claude/hooks/session-start.sh) sets these itself
# in an agent container, so this file is for a laptop or a dev
# container.

# --- The warehouse ----------------------------------------------------
# Where supplies are staged, promoted and checked. Needs a real
# PostgreSQL 16 - the suite refuses to start without one rather than
# skipping, because a suite that skips its warehouse tests reports
# green having checked nothing.
MOTHMAN_SUPPLY_DSN="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/supply"

# The database the TESTS connect to, to create their own throwaway ones
# from. Points at `postgres` rather than at `supply`: each test worker
# gets a database of its own, so this is only the door in.
MOTHMAN_TEST_DSN="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/postgres"

# --- Which deployment this is -----------------------------------------
# One of the ids in contract/environments.yaml (local, sandbox,
# production). There is deliberately no default - a build that guesses
# is a build that can be labelled as somewhere it is not.
MOTHMAN_ENVIRONMENT="local"

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------
# How long to wait for a database lock before giving up, in
# milliseconds. Defaults to 30000. Zero means wait forever, which is
# what PostgreSQL does by default and what turned one leaked connection
# into a six-minute hang.
# MOTHMAN_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS="30000"

# Use a Chromium that is already installed rather than downloading one.
# The agent sandbox ships a build the pinned package does not find.
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_PATH="/opt/pw-browsers/chromium"
